Right on the heels of my last character (geez, don't I have anything better
to do?), another one has ascended....

(usual ascension-oriented spoilers follow)...


Version: PC Nethack 3.1

Class:Samurai, St:21, Dx:23, Co:18, In:22, Wi:22, Ch:9 (snicker)
HP:506/506, Pw:227/293, AC:-50, Xp:30/105360620, T:107945, Score:6146746

Noteworthy items: 4 artifacts (Tsurugi, Grayswandir, Snickersnee, Excalibur),
+4 speed boots, +5 Hawaiian shirt, +4 GDSM, +4 cloak of displacement,
+4 helm of brilliance, +5 gauntlets of dexterity, +3 ring of strength,
blessed amulet of life saving (wasted 2 others seeing what would happen if I
ate Death and Pestilience's corpses... didn't even bother trying Hunger's :-)

I had spells listed down to around C or D by polypiling spellbooks (often
turning up a spellbook of polymorph in the process so I could keep repeating).
And talk about luck, I found a wand of wishing (3 charges) in Gehennom, a
magic marker (62 charges) and managed to get another one via polypiling.  I
already had all the neat armor-type items (speed boots, gauntlets of DEX, 
helm of brilliance) from one of my polypiles, so I was free to just waste
wishes.  I still had the wand I found in Gehennom fully charged when I got to
the Endgame.  In addition, I got intrinsic teleport and teleport control from
the first two tengu corpes I ate.

On the unlucky side, though, I had to try at least 20 times to get up out of
Gehennom, despite wearing a ring of levitation as suggested here.  That is
really annoying, and IMHO doesn't add much to the game.  I also caught a seg
violation on the Plane of Water shortly after putting on my ring of 
levitation to see if I could move more easily.  No big deal, I recovered the
game and refrained from wearing the ring and had no problems afterward.  It
might be something to check out, though.

I loved my stats... 18+ for everything but charisma, which was 7 for most of
the game before finding 2 potions of gain ability late in the game.  I 
picture this bulky superhero type walking around discussing world politics,
the stock market, and proper diet, occasionally checking himself in the 
mirror thinking, "Another zit? *pop!* Ewww!"  Well, he's a demigod now, so
that acne problem should clear right up.
